gaps.proposedFix:
Add to the numeric converter group: `and(k) or(k) not shl(n) shr(n)`.
Encode:  { "u8": "inputs.functionCode | or(0x80)" }
Decode:  { "group":"errPdu", "when":"capture.functionCode | and(0x80) != 0", ... }
and recover the base code with  "capture.functionCode | and(0x7f)". Smallest possible fix — five pure numeric converters, no engine or field-kind change, and it generalises to every protocol with a flag bit packed into a type byte.

Add `mod(n)` to the numeric converter group:
  { "u16be": "seq.next | mod(0x10000)" }
Or parameterise the counter at its source: `seq.next(0x10000)`. Prefer the converter — it is one function and it also serves every protocol with a wrapping frame counter or sequence number.
